  <h1 class="content-title">
    Issue #13 : Garaj
  </h1> 

  <div class="content-text">
  <p><b>Submissions are now open.</b></p> <br>

  <p><i>Garaj</i> (गरज) is Hindi for a roar or thunder. It is the cracking of all that has long been gathering. Where does your thunder begin? Is it in the voice of a student at a barricade, demanding an education that does not discriminate? In the anger of a woman who has to watch her back every time she steps outside? Or is it the first time you raise your voice against a parent, a lover or a tradition that has long called for your silence?</p><br>

  <p>For Issue #13 of <i>The Medley</i>, we invite prose, poetry, essays, and photography that capture the pulse of revolution, in the streets and within the walls of your own home. Thunder can strike fear, but it also brings rain.</p><br>

  <p>When all that has been silenced within you finally breaks, what will your thunder sound like?.</p><br>

  <p>The deadline for submissions is <b>18th December.</b></p>
